{
  "_readme": [
    "The ONE alias layer for every external source (pipeline/external_sheet/aliases.py).",
    "Never hard-code a spelling in a script: add it here, bump `version`, and",
    "rebuild (`python3 pipeline/sheet_sync.py rebuild`).",
    "",
    "Canonical ids come from the published dataset (assets/data/public_data.v1.js:",
    "heroes, mapsCatalog, teams, players) — this file only adds spellings the",
    "published record does not already know. Matching is on normalised text",
    "(lower-case, accents stripped, punctuation removed), so 'Lúcio', 'LUCIO'",
    "and 'lucio' are one spelling already; only list genuinely different ones.",
    "",
    "teams.history handles renamed organisations: a raw name maps to a team id",
    "only inside its validity window, so an old name is never applied to",
    "matches played after it changed hands.",
    "",
    "Reviewed alias approvals made on the Source health page land in",
    "corrections/external_reconciliation.json (aliasApprovals), not here, so",
    "this file stays the hand-curated base and the decisions stay auditable."
  ],
